# Every file is checked out with the bytes the repository holds, on every OS.
#
# Git for Windows checks out text files with CRLF when `core.autocrlf` is
# true, and the CI Windows job's checkout did: recorded fixtures stored with
# LF (`git ls-files --eol`: i/lf) were read with CRLF, so byte comparisons
# with each harness's own output, the plist, the catalog's formatting check
# and the NOTICE tables failed there and nowhere else. Unset `text` means "do
# not attempt any end-of-line conversion upon checkin or checkout"
# (gitattributes(5), https://git-scm.com/docs/gitattributes), whatever
# `core.autocrlf` says. The `.cmd` shims under tests/windows/fixtures are
# stored with CRLF and keep it.
* -text
